    "result": "I've fixed the two rejected gates and the suite passes (31 tests). I haven't run the coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit gates locally, so their results are inferred from the reports rather than measured.\n\n- **CRAP:** `check_password` had complexity 10, which with full coverage gives a CRAP of 10.0. I moved the checks into small helpers, so the function now has a single loop and one `if`, and each helper is simpler.\n- **Mutation survivors:** The `run = 0` survivor was an equivalent mutant in the run-counting loop, so I replaced that loop with an `any()` over consecutive triples. The `return None` survivor disappeared with it. The `<=` survivors on the character-class bounds are now killed by a parametrized test on `a`/`z`, `A`/`Z` and `0`/`9`, each set up so that treating the bound as \"other\" would change the result. The `or`→`and` survivor is killed by tests with a non-string username that would otherwise slip past the type check.",
